  "verbalization": "Metolazone is associated with Vasculitis In The Skin, a condition that is linked to medications such as Methyclothiazide, Irbesartan, and Losartan, all of which are indicated for Hypertensive Disorder. The evidence suggests a potential mechanistic pathway where Metolazone may contribute to the development of Vasculitis In The Skin, which in turn could lead to hypertension. The side-effect relationships indicate that Metolazone may interact with the immune system, potentially triggering vasculitis, which is a known contributor to hypertension in some cases. The final scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple vasculitis-related medications in the pathway highlights the importance of considering drug interactions and side effects in the context of hypertension management.",
